            "normalized_html": "<p>First, notice that <span class=\"math\">[MATH: -\\dfrac{3}{2}=\\dfrac{(-3)}{2}.]</span></p><p>To raise the fraction to the power of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 3]</span>, we must raise both the numerator and the denominator to the power of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 3\\mathbin{:}]</span></p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\left(-\\dfrac{3}{2}\\right)^3=\\left(\\dfrac{(-3)}{2}\\right)^3=\\dfrac{(-3)^3}{2^3}]</span></p><p>Now, computing <span class=\"math\">[MATH: (-3)^3=-27]</span> and <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2^3=8,]</span> we get</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac{(-3)^3}{2^3}= \\dfrac{-27}{8}=-\\dfrac{27}{8} .]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "First, notice that [MATH: -\\dfrac{3}{2}=\\dfrac{(-3)}{2}.]\n\nTo raise the fraction to the power of [MATH: 3], we must raise both the numerator and the denominator to the power of [MATH: 3\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: \\left(-\\dfrac{3}{2}\\right)^3=\\left(\\dfrac{(-3)}{2}\\right)^3=\\dfrac{(-3)^3}{2^3}]\n\nNow, computing [MATH: (-3)^3=-27] and [MATH: 2^3=8,] we get\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac{(-3)^3}{2^3}= \\dfrac{-27}{8}=-\\dfrac{27}{8} .]",
